{"name":"Cherry Plum","hex":"#a10047","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry plum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Prunus cerasifera, a deciduous ornamental Eurasian shrub or small tree, having white flowers and small red to yellow edible fruits.","The fruit of such a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry_plum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus cerasifera","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus cerasifera is a species of plum known by the common names cherry plum and myrobalan plum. Native to Eurasia and naturalized elsewhere, P. cerasifera is believed to be one of the parents of the cultivated plum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Wildpflaume_Althof-2.jpg/330px-Wildpflaume_Althof-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_cerasifera"},{"title":"Plum-cherry hybrid","blocks":[{"text":"A plum-cherry hybrid is a hybrid between Chinese or Japanese plum and sweet cherry. Although it is often called cherry plum, it has no relation to the cherry plum species. It is also known as plerry or cherum. Commercial plum-cherry hybrids include 'Nadia', CherriYum!, Verry Cherry Plum and Pluerry."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum-cherry_hybrid"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_sli